<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alboin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 572</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alboin was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a> from about 560 and led them out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 568, soon after the Gothic Wars had exhausted the peninsula. He conquered much of northern Italy, took Pavia after a long siege and set up the first Lombard duchy at Cividale under his nephew Gisulf. He was murdered at Verona in 572 in a plot involving his wife Rosamund.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alboin.jpg" alt="Alboin" width="219" height="296" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michel Wolgemut, Wilhelm Pleydenwurff (Text: Hartmann Schedel) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nuremberg_chronicles_f_147v_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
